(*!
<summary>Runs a fixed tree of individual tests and nested groups in its owning PLC task.</summary>
<description>
<h2>Configure and run</h2>
Concrete descendants own their persistent root tests, groups and interface-array storage and provide <c>Children</c>.
Construct roots with <c>parent := 0</c>. <c>Parent</c> is the fixed association with a group.
Register each root instance with one runner only. The caller must enforce this because the runner has no parent
marker or registry for detecting shared roots. Keep the <c>Children</c> storage valid and its list unchanged
throughout the runner lifetime.
Call <c>Execute</c> once per PLC cycle until <c>IsFinished</c>. Each run validates roots in <c>STARTING</c>
before any direct reset or report callback. After startup, each call advances at most one leaf body without
repeating topology checks. Empty runs pass with zero tests.

<h2>Read results and recover</h2>
Read the read-only run status and counts from the owning task. Read <c>AllPassed</c> only after <c>IsFinished</c>.
<c>ExitCode</c> is the failed leaf count or <c>-1</c> for a startup failure or an aborted external callback.
Missing storage or null slots raise <c>DataMemberNotSpecifiedException</c>. Duplicate, running or group-owned roots
raise <c>StandardException</c>. <c>Execute</c> catches these startup failures and exposes an aborted run.
An aborted callback is never retried. Counts and report output may be partial.
Make user resources safe before calling <c>Reset</c> after an external abort. <c>Reset</c> does not cancel a run.

<h2>Task and resource ownership</h2>
Use one task without reentry per runner, tree and reporter. Other tasks need disjoint instances and buffers.
Mutable tested resources and custom callbacks also require task isolation or their own synchronization.
The default ADS backend has no established concurrent-call guarantee. Use a separate <c>JUnitXmlReporter</c>
per task for independent in-memory reporting or a reporter backed by a synchronized logging service.
<c>Execute</c> enforces terminal OOM outside recoverable catches. Standalone execution uses
<c>cleanupTaskMemory := TRUE</c> by default to clean the current task after the last consumer of transient exceptions.
Under <c>AutomationRunner</c> or any host that performs this cleanup at the task boundary, pass
<c>cleanupTaskMemory := FALSE</c>.
The runner borrows its children and reporter. Keep dependencies alive while attached and never copy the runner by value.
</description>
*)

{attribute 'no_explicit_call' := 'do not call this function block directly'}
FUNCTION_BLOCK ABSTRACT TestRunner
VAR_GENERIC CONSTANT
	//! <summary>Exact number of root test or group slots.</summary>
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_ChildCount : TOF_Core.INT_LENGTH := 0;
END_VAR
EXTENDS TOF_Core.Object
VAR
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_IsFinished : BOOL;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_AllPassed : BOOL;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_ExitCode : DINT;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_CallbackException : __SYSTEM.ExceptionCode;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_CallbackMessage : TOF_Core.ERROR_MESSAGE;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_TotalTests : TOF_Core.DINT_LENGTH;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_PassedTests : TOF_Core.DINT_LENGTH;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_FailedTests : TOF_Core.DINT_LENGTH;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_SkippedTests : TOF_Core.DINT_LENGTH;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_TotalDuration : TIME;

	_CurrentChildIndex : TOF_Core.INT_LENGTH;
	_Duration : LTIME;
	{attribute 'hide'}
	_Reporter : ITestReporter;
	_DefaultAdsReporter : AdsLogReporter;
	_State : TEST_RUN_PHASE;
END_VAR]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
    <Folder Name="Service members" Id="{24fef69e-e753-4a84-b5d4-f93712c7f5bb}" />
